  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.264,
      "text": "A big Atomy P V number is not a big bank balance.",
      "shot": "Center a huge PV ticket on a blue ground; a money-symbol sticker tries to attach, then is crossed out. Per-word reveal (dynamic-content-sequencing); three layers: dot-grid, ticket, bold crossed symbol. Start with only the ticket, reveal the symbol on bank balance."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.364,
      "end": 10.447,
      "text": "P V means Point Value. Atomy's U S agreement defines it as a measurement used in the compensation plan.",
      "shot": "The same ticket scale-swaps (scale-swap-transition) from PV to POINT VALUE, then unfolds into a tall measuring ruler. Use stacked bands; reveal MEASUREMENT and PLAN on their spoken cues, not at scene start."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.547,
      "end": 16.221,
      "text": "It is not a dollar balance you can withdraw. Commissions still depend on the plan and your eligibility.",
      "shot": "The ruler becomes a receipt with separate POINTS and CASH rows. A withdrawal arrow stops at a black barrier; a QUALIFICATION key arrives later. Sequential disclosure (dynamic-content-sequencing), asymmetric vertical stack, no implied fixed conversion rate."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.321,
      "end": 22.572,
      "text": "So read the label before reading the number. Save this: points measure volume; they do not promise income.",
      "shot": "The receipt contracts to a yellow reminder ticket: READ THE LABEL, then POINTS ≠ PAYDAY. Smooth scale-swap (scale-swap-transition) into an inverted closer; final SAVE THIS tab arrives on Save and holds. Keep the caption band empty."
    }
  ],
